solution:
A system is aromatic only if all of the following hold:

(i) it is planar, so that the p orbitals on every ring atom are parallel and can overlap side by side;

(ii) the \(\pi\) electrons are completely delocalised over a closed, uninterrupted ring (every ring atom must be \(sp^2\) hybridised and carry a p orbital);

(iii) the number of delocalised \(\pi\) electrons in the ring is \((4n+2)\), where \(n = 0, 1, 2, 3, \ldots\) — Huckel's rule.
